# What Vercel gets is a static page, and nothing else in this repo belongs in an upload:
# api/models alone is 3.4 GB of weights and api/venv is another 1.4 GB. This is an
# allowlist - deny everything, then name the few files the build actually reads - so a
# new dataset or checkpoint directory dropped in the tree later cannot silently start
# riding along with the deploy.
*

!Radiology Hub.html
!package.json
!vercel.json
!scripts
!scripts/*

# public/ is this build's own output. Vercel rebuilds it from the page on their machine;
# uploading a locally built copy would just shadow it with whatever was there last.
public/
